          "message": "Acceptance criterion 2 says '`caps.quarantine` folds only the named test'. In the shipped engine, `caps.quarantine` is `Config.caps.quarantine` (squatch/config.py), an integer bound on how many tests can be quarantined at once, and `QUARANTINE_CAP` is a cap name in squatch/caps.py. Neither one folds tests, so the criterion cannot be tested as written. It also leaves unclear whether this ticket owns the section 11.5 cap-crossing behavior (halting further auto-quarantine and escalating). The section 20 flake-boundary clarification this seed cites does not grant that behavior, and it would need an escalation path this fence does not cover.",
